# Sipeed Tang Primer 20K dock, two pins of it.
#
# PROVENANCE: T3 and N16 are balls Project Apicula's own
# `examples/primer20k.cst` names `key_i` and `led[2]`. On the dock, T3 is
# the button silkscreened S4 and N16 the LED silkscreened LED1, which a
# person established on 2026-09-24 by pressing one and watching the other:
# the dock's LED numbering is not Apicula's index.
#
# C13 and A13, which the same file uses for `led[0]` and `led[1]`, are the
# part's DONE and READY pins; `reticle fpga` refuses them as IO, because
# using them so needs a dual-purpose setting this flow does not write.
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 key T3
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led N16
